WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.068
Welcome to the Tepper School of Business.

2
00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:05.305
Home to our undergraduate
and graduate business programs.

3
00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.907
In here, Tepper offers three different majors:

4
00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:11.611
Business Administration
that includes ten different concentrations.

5
00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:15.682
Economics programs with multiple tracks
and computational finance.

6
00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:19.486
The Tepper School here combines
a rigorous analytical approach

7
00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:23.089
to business and economics
with a small and close knit community

8
00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:27.927
to support each other's academics,
leadership and career development from day one.

9
00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.930
All of our Business Administration majors students here

10
00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.999
are required to take a minor as well.

11
00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:36.703
Specifically, Tepper offers
great career exploration programs

12
00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:40.073
to our undergraduate students
here, namely the Tepper Pro Track.

13
00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.741
Students of all different grades

14
00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:45.078
will have the opportunity
to visit different corporate offices

15
00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:48.848
in various industries to hear directly
from full time professionals.

16
00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.384
I went on the Pro Track my very first year here,

17
00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:54.754
and the connections I made back then
even lasted until today.

18
00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:59.092
While we're here, I would also like to point out
the Swartz Center for Entrepreneurship

19
00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.960
that is located on the third floor.

20
00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.765
This center provides funding, mentorship
and resources to all students on campus.

21
00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:09.135
If you're interested in startups
or entrepreneurial mindset,

22
00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:12.238
an application that you may all know,
called Duolingo,

23
00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:15.108
is actually one of the many
startups that originated from here.

24
00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:19.746
I would also like to share about
our classroom experiences here at CMU.

25
00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:23.516
Our overall student to faculty
ratio is 6 to 1

26
00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:26.086
and we have three main
different classroom styles.

27
00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:30.757
The first one is lectures which take place
in big lecture halls with more students.

28
00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:33.993
And then we have recitations
which are smaller sessions

29
00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.329
with more guidance
and hands on approaches.

30
00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:39.566
And lastly, we have office hours
where students can speak

31
00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:42.969
with core staff or faculty
one on one with any questions.

32
00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.170
And with that we will head

33
00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.307
towards our next stop,
which is the School of Computer Science.

